# NOTE: canonical TRACKED copy. The LIVE copy installs to
# /etc/sudoers.d/wingmen-fetch-secrets-wrapper on gzb, owned root:root, mode
# 0440 (matches the existing wingmen-*-restart fragments in /etc/sudoers.d/).
# Install ONLY via `visudo -cf <tmpfile>` validation, never a raw cp -- a
# syntax error in sudoers.d can lock out ALL sudo on the host.
#
# LOCK 1 (Musa op#24409, "never again"). gazzai (the OS user every lane ALSO
# runs as) may run exactly ONE root command, with NO arguments accepted, and
# nothing else. The trailing "" is sudoers' own no-args lockdown (sudoers(5):
# an empty-string Command_Spec arg means the command must be invoked with NO
# arguments) -- a SECOND, independent layer on top of the wrapper's own `$#`
# check (cc-quality bus #48664 #2, MEDIUM: without this, the no-args guarantee
# lived ENTIRELY inside the wrapper script; if the wrapper is ever edited later
# -- a refactor, a dropped early-return, an "optional debug flag" -- the
# sudoers grant would silently become "gazzai can run this root script with
# arbitrary argv" with nothing else catching it). Tested: visudo -cf passes.
gazzai ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/gzb-fetch-secrets-wrapper.sh ""
Defaults!/usr/local/sbin/gzb-fetch-secrets-wrapper.sh !requiretty
